{"diagnosis": "Loopback read got 0xff (all-ones idle) instead of 0xa5, triggering FAIL 0xdead TRAP uart data mismatch. After reset TX is busy with the 15-bit power-on dummy (send_dummy=1, send_bitcnt=15). The extra `if (reg_div_we) send_dummy <= 1` re-arms send_dummy on divider programming, so when the first dummy ends a second dummy starts and blocks `reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt`, dropping 0xa5 and leaving ser_tx idle at 1.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -109,8 +109,6 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
-		if (reg_div_we)
-			send_dummy <= 1;
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP, loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

